{%- comment -%}
  Invisible anti-spam fields. Render immediately inside a {% form %} block and add
  `data-form-guard` to that form tag. Enforcement lives in assets/bould-form-guard.js.

  IMPORTANT: these inputs are deliberately NOT named `contact[...]`. Shopify copies
  every contact[*] field into the notification email, so a contact[]-prefixed field
  would show up in every real submission.

  The honeypot carries no id/label on purpose: {% render %} has an isolated scope, so
  there is no reliable per-form value here to build a unique id from, and duplicate ids
  across forms would be worse than none. The field is off-screen and aria-hidden, so
  assistive tech never reaches it.

  Accepts:
  - min_seconds: {Number} minimum seconds a human is assumed to need (default 3)

  Usage:
  {%- form 'contact', data-form-guard: '' -%}
    {%- render 'form-guard-fields' -%}
  {%- endform -%}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign guard_min_seconds = min_seconds | default: 3 -%}

<div
  aria-hidden="true"
  style="position:absolute!important;left:-9999px!important;top:auto!important;width:1px!important;height:1px!important;overflow:hidden!important;"
>
  <input
    type="text"
    name="bould_website_url"
    value=""
    tabindex="-1"
    autocomplete="off"
    aria-hidden="true"
  >
</div>
<input type="hidden" name="bould_ts" value="" data-guard-min-seconds="{{ guard_min_seconds }}">
